# Argon OS — base system
# Kept deliberately minimal: every package here must justify itself.
# The kernel is selected by live-build itself (--linux-flavours in auto/config).

## Core system
systemd
# systemd-resolved is a separate package now; Argon's DNS-over-TLS setup
# (etc/systemd/resolved.conf.d) depends on it being present and enabled.
systemd-resolved
sudo
apt
apt-transport-https
gnupg
ca-certificates
locales
console-setup
keyboard-configuration
zstd

## Live boot
live-boot
live-config
live-config-systemd
plymouth
plymouth-themes
# label.so — renders ALL text in script-based plymouth themes (Image.Text).
# It is a separate package and only a Recommends, and recommends are
# globally off. Without it Argon's theme still shows the logo but every
# text element renders as nothing — including the LUKS passphrase prompt,
# so an encrypted install boots into an invisible password prompt and
# looks exactly like a hung/failed boot. fonts-dejavu-core provides the
# font the plymouth initramfs hook copies in for label.so to use.
plymouth-label
fonts-dejavu-core

## Firmware (non-free-firmware area; needed for real hardware support)
firmware-linux-free
firmware-misc-nonfree
firmware-realtek
firmware-atheros
firmware-iwlwifi

## Networking
network-manager
wireguard-tools
openvpn

## Security hardening (installed AND enabled by default — see hooks/)
apparmor
apparmor-profiles
apparmor-utils
ufw
fail2ban
unattended-upgrades
apt-listchanges
needrestart

## Privacy
tor
torsocks
mat2
chrony

## Secure remote access (installed but disabled by default — see hooks/)
openssh-client
openssh-server

## Base utilities
bash-completion
curl
wget
git
vim
nano
htop
less
man-db
rsync
unzip
p7zip-full
cryptsetup
# Unlocks the encrypted root from the initramfs at boot. It is only a
# Recommends of cryptsetup (and recommends are globally off), so without
# listing it an encrypted install would finish fine and then never boot.
cryptsetup-initramfs
btrfs-progs
dosfstools
gparted
